{"kind": "mod", "id": 2278, "name": "Caliber Split Magazine Cases", "slug": "caliber-split-magazine-cases", "teaser": "Organize your magazines with caliber-specific cases for easier management!", "owner_name": "Szonszczyk", "downloads": 6991, "favourites": 9, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.szonszczyk.calibersplitmagazinecases", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Items", "category_id": 4, "updated_at": "2026-07-28T09:22:33.000000Z", "created_at": "2025-09-01T09:55:23.000000Z", "published_at": "2025-09-01T09:55:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0.0", "latest_version": "2.0.2", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p>Adds procedurally generated magazine cases split by caliber, adapting automatically to the mods and magazines available on your server.</p>\n<p>Each magazine is assigned to its caliber case based on the ammo it can hold.</p>\n<p>A detailed config file allows you to customize case sizes.</p>\n<h3><strong>Features</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatically generates cases for all magazines in the game (including modded ones, excluding internal magazines)</li>\n<li>Cases can be added to traders: Skier (EUR), Peacekeeper (USD), Ref (GP Coin), Jaeger (RUB), or Prapor (barter)</li>\n<li>Config options for background color, width, height and price of cases</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><strong>Compatibility</strong></h3>\n<p>Fully compatible with all mods that add magazines to the game. Load this mod after all magazine-adding mods for proper function.</p>\n<p>For best results (correct caliber names and filtering out invalid/unneeded ones), review the config file.</p>\n<h3><strong>Credits</strong></h3>\n<p>Part of typescript codebase by GroovypenguinX</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/52v5cYN.png\" alt=\"52v5cYN.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"